<hr class="rule rule--heavy">

{# The two-door fork. Rendered as stacked entries rather than a side-by-side
   pair: there is no 2-up component in the system today and inventing one is a
   DESIGN-SYSTEM decision, not a page decision. The doors are in-page anchors —
   /learn/editor/ and /learn/cartography/ are article URLs, not sub-hubs, and
   inventing hub URLs would create shipped-URL obligations nobody asked for. #}
<section class="section">
  <a href="#make" class="guide-entry">
    <div class="guide-entry__overline">Door one</div>
    <div class="guide-entry__title">Make a map</div>
    <div class="guide-entry__description">Short, specific how-tos for the Atelier: choosing colors, applying patterns, styling borders, adding places, sharing what you made. Follow one and you have a finished map at the end.</div>
  </a>
  <a href="#understand" class="guide-entry">
    <div class="guide-entry__overline">Door two</div>
    <div class="guide-entry__title">Understand maps</div>
    <div class="guide-entry__description">Why a palette holds together or falls apart, what a map is allowed to leave out, when a pattern beats a pin. Ideas you can use anywhere, not just here.</div>
  </a>
</section>

{# Each track's section only exists when it has something in it. An emitted-
   but-empty section is not neutral here: `.section + .section` draws a top
   border, so a heading with nothing under it reads as a broken page. #}
